/-! Data of the bitset certificate for the Seventh binary forest.

The 35 roots are one point of each orbit of the group generated by the four Seventh forest
letters on the singular binary masks: zero, eleven short classes and 23 type-four classes.
The 25 doubling steps are words in the four letters together with row operations
computing the binary matrix of each word. All data are discovery outputs; the kernel checks every
use, through the generic bitset operations `tenthForestDouble` and `tenthForestOpsMap`. -/

@[expose] public section
namespace FormalizedTextbooks.FrenkelLepowskyMeurmanMonster

